<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		This file exists for the keys that are arrays. Every other Info.plist value for this
		target still comes from GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE and the INFOPLIST_KEY_ build settings,
		which Xcode merges into this file at build time; the INFOPLIST_KEY_ mechanism carries
		strings and booleans only. It sits beside the target's folder rather than inside it
		because a synchronized root group copies its own files into the bundle, and Xcode 26
		cannot read a project whose exception set is attached to a target's own synchronized root
		group; the Mac target's exception list, which already names every ThreadingMobile file,
		is the one mechanism that works for both.

		Without NSBonjourServices, browsing for the service fails silently on iOS 14 and later:
		no results, no error, no prompt. MobileLocalNetworkPermissionTests asserts the built app
		carries it, because "silently finds nothing" is not a symptom anybody debugs quickly.
	-->
	<key>NSBonjourServices</key>
	<array>
		<string>_threading._tcp</string>
	</array>
	<!--
		The scheme an invitation is addressed to.

		A one-chat invitation points at a private door on somebody's LAN or tailnet, with the
		Mac's own certificate fingerprint in the fragment. Sent as the bare https URL it opened
		in Safari, which can only offer the certificate interstitial: the pin that makes that
		door trustworthy lives in this app and a browser has no way to learn it. `threading://`
		is how the invitation reaches the app that holds the pin. `PAIR` was already the QR
		payload's scheme (`HostedPairingLink`); registering it here is what makes a tap work as
		well as a photograph, and `JOIN` carries the same https invitation, fragment and all.

		Lower case: schemes are case-insensitive (RFC 3986 §3.1), so the upper-case QR payloads
		still route here. MobileInvitationRouteTests asserts the built app carries it.
	-->
	<key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
			<string>Viewer</string>
			<key>CFBundleURLName</key>
			<string>codes.threading.mobile.invitation</string>
			<key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
			<array>
				<string>threading</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
